<section class="intro">
    <p>
        We run this mic as a safer and more welcoming space, especially for queer folks and women.
        Everyone is welcome when they can respect the room, the lineup, and each other.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="events-section">
    <h2>Event Rules & Expectations</h2>

    <div class="event-card">
        <div class="event-title">For Performers</div>
        <div class="event-details">
            <div class="event-detail-item">
                <span>Performers of all identities are welcome to perform, but please be respectful of the audience and the room.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="event-detail-item">
                <span>Harassment, hate speech, or targeted cruelty toward individuals based on their identity is not allowed. Don't be a jerk.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="event-detail-item">
                <span>Crowdwork is allowed, but if you are asked to stop, please do so immediately. Consent is required.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="event-detail-item">
                <span>If you are a performer and you are uncomfortable with a joke, please let the host know immediately.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="event-detail-item">
                <span>Respect your set length and the host's timing calls so the night runs smoothly.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="event-detail-item">
                <span>Hosts may cut sets or skip performers if rules are ignored. Repeat violations can mean removal from future mics.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="event-card stacked-card">
        <div class="event-title">For Audience Members</div>
        <div class="event-details">
            <div class="event-detail-item">
                <span>Be kind and present. Listen while performers are on stage and keep side conversations to a minimum.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="event-detail-item">
                <span>No heckling, harassment, or threatening behavior.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="event-detail-item">
                <span>Honor names, pronouns, and boundaries. If someone tells you a boundary, respect it immediately.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="event-detail-item">
                <span>If something feels unsafe, find the host or organizer right away. We will listen and act.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="event-card stacked-card">
        <div class="event-title">Accountability & Safety</div>
        <div class="event-details">
            <div class="event-detail-item">
                <span>Organizers can warn, remove, or deny entry to anyone who violates these expectations.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="event-detail-item">
                <span>Safety calls are made to protect the room, this is a safe space first and foremost. We appreciate your cooperation.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="event-detail-item">
                <span>If you need to report an issue privately, email us at <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
